[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m The problem involves two congruent squares each with side length 12, forming a rectangle AEHD with dimensions 12 by 20. We need the percentage of the area of rectangle AEHD that is shaded (which is the overlapping area).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m 1. Each square has area \(12 \times 12 = 144\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m 2. Two squares have a combined area of \(2 \times 144 = 288\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m 3. The formed rectangle AEHD has area \(12 \times 20 = 240\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m 4. The overlapping area is therefore \(288 - 240 = 48\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m 5. The percentage shaded (if the overlapping area is shaded) is \(\frac{48}{240} \times 100 = 20\%\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1799)[0m Thus, the final answer is \(\boxed{20}\).
